*==============================================================
*  THE SAME TEN OFF-GRID STATES WITH CUBIC INTERPOLATION.
*  Added 2026-10-02.  LINEAR came out at 30.4 pcm worst against a 30 pcm
*  gate, and the two worst points are both in the intervals the widened axes
*  created -- which is where the Doppler dependence is steepest in curvature,
*  because k varies roughly as sqrt(TF) and the second derivative is largest
*  at the cold end.  Linear interpolation error goes as (dx)^2 f'', so a
*  NARROW interval can still be the worst one if it sits where f'' is large.
*  CUBIC costs nothing but a keyword and no rebuild, so the question is
*  whether it buys the margin back.  Same states, same references.
*==============================================================

EVALUATE bu dca tf tg := 0.0 0.66 750.0 625.0 ;
Macro := NCR: Cpo :: EDIT 0 MACRO CUBIC NMIX 1 COMPO Cpo 'EDIRBMK'
  MIX 1 FROM 1 SET 'burnup' <<bu>> SET 'DCA' <<dca>>
               SET 'TF' <<tf>> SET 'TG' <<tg>> ENDMIX ;
SYSTEM := TRIVAA: Macro TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
FLUX   := FLUD: SYSTEM TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
GREP: FLUX :: GETVAL 'K-EFFECTIVE' 1 >>kinf<< ;
ECHO "A5BSWEEPCUB" bu dca tf tg kinf ;
Macro SYSTEM FLUX := DELETE: Macro SYSTEM FLUX ;

EVALUATE bu dca tf tg := 0.0 0.085 1750.0 825.0 ;
