*--------------------------------------------------------------
*  AXIS DECOMPOSITION, added 2026-10-02.
*  LINEAR interpolation came out at 30.4 pcm against a 30 pcm gate, and
*  the two worst points are both at (DCA 0.76, TF 565) -- inside the two
*  intervals the widened axes created.  CUBIC is not the answer: it cuts
*  the error at BU 0 but takes it to -48 pcm at BU 20000, and NCR.f:139
*  has one global LCUBIC flag, so it cannot be chosen per axis.
*  Before widening a grid, find out WHICH axis is paying.  These five
*  states are off-grid in exactly one axis at a time, at BU 0 where the
*  error was worst, so the 30.4 pcm can be decomposed instead of guessed.
*--------------------------------------------------------------

*  all three on grid: the deck path itself
EVALUATE bu dca tf tg := 0.0 0.80 600.0 750.0 ;
Macro := NCR: Cpo :: EDIT 0 MACRO LINEAR NMIX 1 COMPO Cpo 'EDIRBMK'
  MIX 1 FROM 1 SET 'burnup' <<bu>> SET 'DCA' <<dca>>
               SET 'TF' <<tf>> SET 'TG' <<tg>> ENDMIX ;
SYSTEM := TRIVAA: Macro TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
FLUX   := FLUD: SYSTEM TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
GREP: FLUX :: GETVAL 'K-EFFECTIVE' 1 >>kinf<< ;
ECHO "A5BSWEEPAXIS" bu dca tf tg kinf ;
Macro SYSTEM FLUX := DELETE: Macro SYSTEM FLUX ;

*  DCA only, inside the NEW 0.72..0.80 interval
EVALUATE bu dca tf tg := 0.0 0.76 600.0 750.0 ;
Macro := NCR: Cpo :: EDIT 0 MACRO LINEAR NMIX 1 COMPO Cpo 'EDIRBMK'
  MIX 1 FROM 1 SET 'burnup' <<bu>> SET 'DCA' <<dca>>
               SET 'TF' <<tf>> SET 'TG' <<tg>> ENDMIX ;
SYSTEM := TRIVAA: Macro TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
FLUX   := FLUD: SYSTEM TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
GREP: FLUX :: GETVAL 'K-EFFECTIVE' 1 >>kinf<< ;
ECHO "A5BSWEEPAXIS" bu dca tf tg kinf ;
Macro SYSTEM FLUX := DELETE: Macro SYSTEM FLUX ;

*  TF only, inside the NEW 530..600 interval
EVALUATE bu dca tf tg := 0.0 0.80 565.0 750.0 ;
Macro := NCR: Cpo :: EDIT 0 MACRO LINEAR NMIX 1 COMPO Cpo 'EDIRBMK'
  MIX 1 FROM 1 SET 'burnup' <<bu>> SET 'DCA' <<dca>>
               SET 'TF' <<tf>> SET 'TG' <<tg>> ENDMIX ;
SYSTEM := TRIVAA: Macro TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
FLUX   := FLUD: SYSTEM TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
GREP: FLUX :: GETVAL 'K-EFFECTIVE' 1 >>kinf<< ;
ECHO "A5BSWEEPAXIS" bu dca tf tg kinf ;
Macro SYSTEM FLUX := DELETE: Macro SYSTEM FLUX ;

*  TG only, the old 500..750 interval
EVALUATE bu dca tf tg := 0.0 0.80 600.0 625.0 ;
Macro := NCR: Cpo :: EDIT 0 MACRO LINEAR NMIX 1 COMPO Cpo 'EDIRBMK'
  MIX 1 FROM 1 SET 'burnup' <<bu>> SET 'DCA' <<dca>>
               SET 'TF' <<tf>> SET 'TG' <<tg>> ENDMIX ;
SYSTEM := TRIVAA: Macro TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
FLUX   := FLUD: SYSTEM TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
GREP: FLUX :: GETVAL 'K-EFFECTIVE' 1 >>kinf<< ;
ECHO "A5BSWEEPAXIS" bu dca tf tg kinf ;
Macro SYSTEM FLUX := DELETE: Macro SYSTEM FLUX ;

*  DCA+TF, both new intervals, TG on grid
EVALUATE bu dca tf tg := 0.0 0.76 565.0 750.0 ;
Macro := NCR: Cpo :: EDIT 0 MACRO LINEAR NMIX 1 COMPO Cpo 'EDIRBMK'
  MIX 1 FROM 1 SET 'burnup' <<bu>> SET 'DCA' <<dca>>
               SET 'TF' <<tf>> SET 'TG' <<tg>> ENDMIX ;
SYSTEM := TRIVAA: Macro TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
FLUX   := FLUD: SYSTEM TRACK :: EDIT 0 ;
GREP: FLUX :: GETVAL 'K-EFFECTIVE' 1 >>kinf<< ;
ECHO "A5BSWEEPAXIS" bu dca tf tg kinf ;
Macro SYSTEM FLUX := DELETE: Macro SYSTEM FLUX ;

*  BURNUP OFF-GRID (2026-10-02).  The core runs at 10 900 MWd/t, between the
*  10 000 and 12 500 nodes, so the burnup axis is interpolated in every core
*  calculation.  The first version of this test used 500, 3500 and 17 500 and
*  found +2099 pcm at 500; those three are COMPO NODES as of the same day's
*  rebuild, so they would now test nothing.  The two points below are the ones
*  the rebuild deliberately left off the node set: 250, in the steepest part
*  of the curve where the xenon knee lives, and 11 250, in the interval the
*  core itself runs in.  DCA/TF/TG are held on the grid so the error is the
*  burnup axis's alone.

*--------------------------------------------------------------
*  ROUND TRIP AT THE NEW AXIS VALUES, added 2026-10-02.
*  The eight round-trip nodes above were chosen for the 840-point table and
*  none of them lands on DCA 0.80 or TF 530 -- the two values the 2026-10-01
*  rebuild added.  The branch table holds 144 rows at 0.80 and 192 at 530, so
*  DRAGON computed them; what was never checked is that NCR: READS THEM BACK.
*  A new axis value is exactly where a storage or ordering mistake would hide,
*  and these four cost nothing: the references are already in the table.
*--------------------------------------------------------------

EVALUATE bu dca tf tg := 0.0 0.80 530.0 500.0 ;
Macro := NCR: Cpo :: EDIT 0 MACRO LINEAR NMIX 1 COMPO Cpo 'EDIRBMK'
  MIX 1 FROM 1 SET 'burnup' <<bu>> SET 'DCA' <<dca>>
               SET 'TF' <<tf>> SET 'TG' <<tg>> ENDMIX ;
